  "body": "## Accepted boundedness partial, attempt 1/5\n\nProblem 11000150 / AMR-109-0150, rank 1256. For each fixed genus g >= 1, positive factorizations of one boundary twist with pairwise geometric intersection at most one form finitely many simultaneous-conjugacy classes and have a finite attained length maximum. Repetitions are allowed, disk-bounding twists excluded, and all mapping classes preserve orientation and fix the sole boundary pointwise. The broader boundary-parallel convention is retained and analyzed.\n\nThe complete report and audit preserve the right-veering positivity argument, exact deletion algebra, self-contained finite-alphabet Higman proof, mod-two support bound, finite ribbon-graph/complement orbit proof and centrality step. The separating-factor exclusion includes the full capped Lefschetz-fibration construction, (-1) section and homologically nonzero fibre needed for the credited Smith theorem. Prior results are explicitly credited, including M(1)=12 and M(2)=40 and generic Higman-based factorization methods.\n\nThe arbitrary-length subquestion is answered negatively in fixed genus. The exact maximum for g >= 3, an explicit numerical upper bound and extremizer classifications remain unresolved. No Hurwitz, positive-Artin, T-move or A5/D6 classification is claimed. The distinct-support bound is not a factorization-length bound; no effective exhaustive-search stopping rule is supplied.\n\n## Publication boundary and review limits\n\nExactly six authored proof/audit/status and public-source-metadata files are added under `unsolved_math_prioritization/attempts/11000150/`. Full symbolic arguments and mathematical examples are retained. Programs, computational sections/results, fixtures, imported dataset contents, copied third-party source bodies and private coordination material are excluded. No excluded computation is rewritten as prose.\n\nThis AI-assisted, unrefereed edition claims no historical novelty, priority, current-openness certification, external human peer review, journal acceptance or formal proof-assistant certification. Recorded source retrieval and inspection are historical observations. Edition preparation makes no new scholarly retrieval, PDF rehash, source inspection or literature-search claim.\n\nQUEUE.md and unrelated entries remain unchanged. Editorial preparation adds no substantive proof turn and does not reset attempt 1/5. No merge, release, DOI or outside outreach is requested.\n\nBase commit: `f6caddda8f8be2cdb3e91494325d8f7f365bc3fc`.\n\n## Exact distributed file identities\n\n- `MANIFEST.json`: 1,293 bytes; SHA-256 `f6dc80aa326c5bb550d6ba0f7ed7d3c4d67a5487f72fdff5ef1c3560633fcd98`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_AUDIT.md`: 16,278 bytes; SHA-256 `b8b5715645bbe32426bb6683f68e7c07b4e2ec28d282e9b0a509ec54de3c0b9f`.\n- `MATHEMATICAL_REPORT.md`: 22,957 bytes; SHA-256 `eeb44a07e7503985ef466b882f969b27485f47536c0057ea14163d4b68759db3`.\n- `README.md`: 4,215 bytes; SHA-256 `bff44ae48f38c1323910b14282942eec4adc5ea94a7237a9ccc1f704766f97ac`.\n- `SOURCE_METADATA.json`: 7,277 bytes; SHA-256 `69abacf4bfab9d6089b9e7d760db5f99d1a07e25d8ce49b2a8ca3c29218a4d7c`.\n- `STATUS.json`: 2,411 bytes; SHA-256 `dad949eb386681860f3239a8046857637b323eacc6d549d86473831b69f4c35f`.\n\nThe manifest lists six members and hashes the other five; this body pins the manifest independently.\n",
